{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-tirewear-fixture",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.1's per-fixture document, at fixture scale: `process-tirewear` as a thin document mounting a shared one. It holds no data, no shape, no metaparameters, no enums and no logic — only this metadata and one top-level `models` entry that is a `{ref}` to `tirewear_mount.esm`, which carries the 51 `data_sources` and mounts `onroad/model.esm` in turn. Three documents and two mount edges, emitting the same 375 rows as the inlined `fixtures/process-tirewear.esm`, byte for byte.\n\nWHY IT COULD NOT EXIST BEFORE 2026-09-14. The loader API bound a `data_source`'s discovered `extent` only at the ROOT document, so the root had to declare every metaparameter those extents bind — here 48 names and 247 lines that configured nothing, in every fixture — even though the logic half declares the same names and owns the axes they size (finding F50). EarthSciAST PR #317 binds a discovered extent in whichever document of the assembly declares the name, at either mount form and transitively, so this document declares none.\n\nIT WAS 43 LINES UNTIL 2026-09-17, and 31 of those were an enum union the build never needed. They were restated because `tools/check-conventions.py` required every assembly to carry the union of what it mounts: enums merged first-wins across a mount and a same-name symbol at a different value was applied silently (finding F13). EarthSciAST PR #353 resolves a mounted file's `enum` ops against that file's own block, so a leaf reads its own symbol whatever this document says, and the block is deleted. What is left is the whole of what a per-fixture document has to carry.\n\nWHAT IT DOES NOT DO YET is configure anything. It mounts the only catalogue this fixture has, the process snapshot. The document PLAN.md §7.5 step 7c′ wants reads the monolithic default database from the shared document and carries only this fixture's runspec selections here; that needs the generators upstream of tire wear ported, and is the next step rather than this one.\n\nHOW IT IS CHECKED. run-tests.sh's 7c stage emits this document's relation and compares it byte for byte with the inlined fixture's output from the same run, exactly as it does for `tirewear_mount.esm`, and asserts that this document declares no `data_sources`, `metaparameters`, `index_sets` or model of its own — so it cannot grow back into a mechanical copy without the suite saying so."
  },
  "models": {
    "Onroad": {
      "ref": "./tirewear_mount.esm"
    }
  }
}
